## Question

How do the repository README and the listing README read and look, from the first screen to the last? Which card does a shared link unfold into?

Draft with `/prototype` on a `prototype/readme` branch and react. The drafts use the words [#117 What does Hero Synergy say about itself?](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/issues/117) decides, the shots and loop from [#116 Capture the real Cockpit in screenshots and a loop](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/issues/116), the files from [#118 Cut the trailer for the web](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/issues/118) and the patterns from [#115 How do the best developer-tool READMEs and extension listings open?](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/issues/115):

- **First screen.** Two or three variants: the trailer first, the real Cockpit loop first, or the banner over one screenshot. Centred or left-aligned. Which badges earn their place.
- **Repository README.** What it adds beyond the listing:
  - how it works, with a diagram: the scout reads the tracker into a snapshot, and the status plugin's hooks and Claude Code's registry report each session;
  - the packages;
  - how Hero Synergy was itself charted and built with wayfinder maps: [#1 hero-synergy v0.1.0, fully decided](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/issues/1), [#37 Spec: hero-synergy v0.1.0, the Cockpit](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/issues/37), [#64 next, the terminal pre-alpha of the Cockpit](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/issues/64) and this map;
  - developing, credits and the licence.
- **Listing README.** From install to the first ticket session:
  - requirements;
  - a quick start: install the skills, Setup, Chart a map, ▶ on a frontier ticket;
  - a tour of the Tree, the Focus pane and the Detail;
  - live status and the badge;
  - settings, commands and conventions;
  - troubleshooting with the Health row and the output channel.
- **The trailer beside the Cockpit.** Where it plays, and how it is captioned so that its board is not read as the product. Also what happens to the two claims a caption cannot fix: the "+ CLI" outro, and the typed command without its `#<number>`, which [#115 How do the best developer-tool READMEs and extension listings open?](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/issues/115) found.
- **Social card.** One of the candidates from [#118 Cut the trailer for the web](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/issues/118), or a new one.
- **Media.** Where each file lives in the repository, the URL each README uses for it, and its alt text.

Render both drafts for the reaction: the repository README on the branch's GitHub page, and the listing in the Extensions view from a packaged VSIX. The resolution records what was chosen. The branch holds the drafts that [#121 Land the front door and release it](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/issues/121) ships.

## Context

- [`docs/brand.md`](https://github.com/dbarjs/hero-synergy/blob/main/docs/brand.md): the root README can show `packages/vscode/media/icon.svg` by relative path, and the listing needs absolute `https://` PNG URLs.
- HITL: Eduardo reacts to the drafts.

